plit so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add to the ADR an explicit novelty/prior-art justification for the single-agent engine: why its omission of Pass-2 verify and Pass-3 decide is acceptable for plan review, how it relates to ADR 0075 (which retired a single-pass code-review route for lacking exactly those passes), and why the agentic verdict is trustworthy without them.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan section 3: 'The agentic engine has no Pass-2 verify or Pass-3 decide step, so no priority or decision margin is computed; those fields are absent, as they are for DET findings.'","docs/adr/0075-retire-single-pass-code-review.md:13-17: the retired single-pass code-review route had 'NO Pass-2 verifier, NO deterministic Pass-3 decision, NO Pass-4 coaching — none of the four-pass review kernel's guarantees,' and keeping two paths was called a 'half-migration.'","Retrieved web prior art (looksgoodtomeow.in 'AI code review — explained'; pickuma.com 'AdamsReview multi-agent PR review'): single-agent review is 'simpler/cheaper per review' but multi-pass 'catches what single-pass LLM reviews miss' — a recognized architectural tradeoff.","ABSENCE: the ADR's framing treats the second engine as a parent-epic premise; neither the Approach nor an (implied) Consequences section weighs the single-agent engine's reduced rigor against the pipeline or reconciles it with ADR 0075."],"finding":"The ADR introduces a single-agent plan-review engine that deliberately omits Pass-2 verify and Pass-3 decide, but does not justify this novel (less-rigorous) topology against the established 4-pass pipeline or engage the repo's own on-point prior art (ADR 0075) that retired a single-pass review route for exactly that missing rigor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f436ecf7960580f8a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, section 2 (Agentic engine design) and section 3 (Severity-to-verdict mapping)","norm_id":"nacbb453a1823ac92","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later reader of docs/adr/ evaluates whether the agentic engine should ever supersede the pipeline (the sunset ticket referenced by the mechanism-ok marker) with no recorded rationale for accepting a verify/decide-free verdict path.","An operator choosing the (D) default weighs engine selection without the ADR stating why a single-agent verdict is trustworthy absent Pass-2/Pass-3."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In section 2 (or a Consequences/Alternatives subsection), state the tradeoff the single-agent topology makes vs the 4-pass pipeline, cite ADR 0075 and distinguish plan review's case (e.g., the Layer-1 floor + claimability gating in section 6 and severity-only mapping in section 3 as the rigor substitutes), so the reduced-rigor engine is a recorded, reconciled decision rather than an unexplained divergence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects